message.content:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a “flip‑card” that rotates around its vertical axis when you hover over it.  
All the magic happens in CSS – no JavaScript required.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Obracająca się karta</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Set up the outer wrapper */
.card {
    width: 300px;          /* adjust as needed */
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 1000px;   /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
    margin: 50px auto;     /* center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  Inner container that will actually flip */
.card-inner {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform 0.6s;      /* smooth animation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;    /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* 3️⃣  Flip on hover */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* 4️⃣  Front face */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;     /* hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card-front {
    background: #fff;
    color: #333;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    padding: 20px;
}

/* 5️⃣  Back face – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card-back {
    background: #f8f9fa;
    color: #222;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);       /* start flipped */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    padding: 20px;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <h2>Front</h2>
            <p>To jest przednia strona karty.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <h2>Back</h2>
            <p>To jest tylna strona karty.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `.card` sets a `perspective`, creating a 3‑D context for its children. |
| **2** | `.card-inner` holds both faces and has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its children stay in 3‑D space. |
| **3** | Hovering over `.card` triggers a rotation of `.card-inner` by 180° along the Y‑axis. |
| **4** | `.card-front` is the visible side initially. |
| **5** | `.card-back` is rotated 180° so it’s hidden until the parent flips. |

Feel free to replace the placeholder text or add images, icons, or other styling to suit your design. Adjust the `width`, `height`, and `font-size` values to fit your layout.
